{"id": "EUVD-2026-86044", "enisaUuid": "d26fe04d-2670-3a65-9c16-4746b6a70e9b", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndrm/amd/display: Avoid DPMS-on for phantom stream\n\n[Why & How]\nCalling dc_update_planes_and_stream separately for stream and its\nphantom stream causes a NULL pointer dereference, since the phantom is\ndestroyed on the first call.\n\nSkip the call for phantom streams.", "datePublished": "2026-09-24T16:03:44", "dateUpdated": "2026-09-25T12:44:07", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f2463fc246d3c39be1371389c52b29418ad673d0", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/10f5f9c0ef32d08b228bfee3684b62f36f395852"], "aliases": ["GHSA-f7rg-9g9x-q35j", "CVE-2026-97431"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.16, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "091c3a41-6974-36c3-8a83-4ef6f25a860c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.17"}, {"id": "3080ccde-cccc-3c34-a17b-d65174bc638a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.53"}, {"id": "57684162-829d-312a-8daf-bcabe26b47f7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2"}, {"id": "ab161ab1-ee49-3466-84c8-f2630c90e7a7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "9c6669c2e21a2d9b3f3857883c715a302ae64ac0 <10f5f9c0ef32d08b228bfee3684b62f36f395852"}, {"id": "bd770a22-a58a-355b-9a38-945da10c9e75", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "9c6669c2e21a2d9b3f3857883c715a302ae64ac0 <f2463fc246d3c39be1371389c52b29418ad673d0"}, {"id": "e1fb2af3-5e4b-3539-a263-7f8a9abb3afe", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "89eed3f3-de2f-317b-b319-0b8b64176e94", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}